  "answer": "Citation complaints dropped sharply from Q1 to Q2 after the April 2026 fix. Q1 had a sharp increase in citation-error tickets, with issues like incorrect file links, missing page numbers, empty citations, and broken links [NL-010#NL-010-S05]. Monthly citation-accuracy tickets fell from 88 in March to 42 in April, then 31 in May and 24 in June, after the April release bound document metadata directly to vector chunks [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. The remaining scanned-document problem is directly addressed by the planned Advanced OCR Pipeline, scheduled for release in August 2026, which will integrate an OCR engine into the KnowledgeHub ingestion queue and extract text and layout structures from scanned, image-only PDFs to enable page-specific citations [NL-010#NL-010-S10] [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
